# Licensing and third-party notices

Original ACE CDL Explorer code is licensed under MIT (LICENSE). Third-party
material retains the following upstream licenses; the MIT grant does not
relicense that material. Keep these notices in source and binary distributions.

- The bundled CXF-Core interfaces and pinned modelica-json fixtures originate at
  modelica-json revision f75058d25bafb8c503e894dd193d3fa8037aef23. The complete
  upstream license is reproduced below, including its enhancements paragraph.
- Modelica Buildings/OBC source files, reference results and source-derived
  control sequences originate at modelica-buildings revision
  d3d8e6f76514dfbc7d65574c6b5a777b686fe1b7. The complete upstream License.mo
  is reproduced below, including copyright, funding notice and additional terms.
- The native funnel implementation uses independent interpolation/window-extrema
  code. pyfunnel remains a separately installed verification tool, not a linked
  or redistributed component of these crates.

The two upstream licenses permit source/binary redistribution with their notices,
conditions, disclaimers and non-endorsement terms retained. This distribution
retains the complete text rather than substituting the standard BSD template.
No upstream names or marks confer endorsement.

